# Internal working docs — must never be served publicly.
#
# CLAUDE.md   pricing rationale, launch strategy, unbuilt security plans
# CONTEXT.md  business validation notes, the open questions list, and the fact
#             that this started with Lamont's autistic niece — family detail
#             that is nobody else's business
# VOICE.md    how we talk about the reader; reads badly if the reader finds it
# SCOPE.md    the licensing boundary and the reasoning behind it — internal legal
#             thinking, not a customer document
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
VOICE.md
SCOPE.md

# Database setup script. Nothing secret in it, but it maps the schema and
# bucket rules — no reason to hand that to anyone who guesses the filename.
supabase-setup.sql
supabase-setup-2.sql

# Internal docs for the free resource platform.
# RESOURCE.md          the rules for everything under /start/
# platform-design.html the design rationale — internal thinking, not a customer document
# facts.json           source of truth for every date, deadline and phone number.
#                      Phase 0 adds a loader that reads this at runtime; when that
#                      lands, facts.json has to come OUT of this list so it can be
#                      served. The other two stay ignored forever.
docs/RESOURCE.md
docs/platform-design.html

# The resource platform itself, in draft. Not servable: all 22 entries in
# facts.json are status "unverified", all 9 translations are "draft", and none of
# these pages carries a noindex tag. Nothing here goes in front of a family until
# a human verifies the facts against primary sources. Phase 0 splits these into
# per-question pages under /start/, /es/start/ and /ht/start/.

# The test suites. They are developer tools that run on a laptop against the
# files on disk and against prod; nothing on the site loads them, and every one
# of them was being SERVED at https://kirtonlearning.com/verify/*.mjs — a
# readable map of the token rules, the admin actions and the DNS setup, handed to
# anyone who guesses the filename. Same reasoning as supabase-setup.sql above.
# (The repo is public, so this hides nothing that is secret. It stops the
# customer domain from volunteering it.)
verify/
